From: Luisyr <106528106+luisyr1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:08:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/11] drm/panel: add a minimal Google KM4 panel driver
 (brightness only)

The Pixel 9 Pro XL's KM4 (SLSI DDIC, bootloader name google-km4) runs as
ABL left it. Expose its brightness as a backlight device through the
gs-dsim-cmd DSI host: DCS 0x51 with a big-endian 16-bit level inside
Google's normal range (176..3271, default 1209), pixel off (0x22) at 0
and normal mode (0x13) to leave it, as Google's panel-gs-km4.c does. No
init sequence, no 0xF0-unlocked vendor register, no reset or supplies,
no rate switch. Sleep in/out and display on/off are drm_panel hooks only,
for a display driver with the panel on its output port.

Every write goes through gs-dsim-cmd, which refuses it with -EPERM until
gs_dsim_cmd.allow_tx=1; the driver then only keeps the level.

Not tested on hardware.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig            |  12 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Makefile           |   1 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-google-km4.c | 279 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 kernel/configs/komodo-display.config     |   3 +
 4 files changed, 295 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-google-km4.c

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig
index d82882275..51d47f7a3 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig
@@ -225,6 +225,18 @@ config DRM_PANEL_GOOGLE_HK3
 	  running, switches it between 60 and 120 Hz, puts it to sleep and
 	  exposes its brightness as a backlight.
 
+config DRM_PANEL_GOOGLE_KM4
+	tristate "Google KM4 DSI command mode panel (brightness only)"
+	depends on OF
+	depends on DRM_MIPI_DSI
+	depends on BACKLIGHT_CLASS_DEVICE
+	help
+	  Say Y or M here if you want to control the Google KM4 1344x2992
+	  command-mode AMOLED panel, found in the Google Pixel 9 Pro XL.
+	  The driver takes over the panel the bootloader left running and
+	  exposes its brightness as a backlight; it sends no initialisation
+	  sequence and does not switch the refresh rate.
+
 config DRM_PANEL_GOOGLE_TG4C
 	tristate "Google TG4C DSI command mode panel"
 	depends on OF
